        "id": 1061116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-23T13:20:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe the API name is not right. The Binder.getCallingUid isn\u0027t in all cases the right caller. In particular if you perform a recheck as part of app update you come from a different call path.",
      "parentUuid": "8e08466f_3e1bb4a5",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1f8129a_251cae51",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1431994
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T16:50:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What would that call path be? I\u0027d still prefer we restrict what sort of callers can do this.",
      "parentUuid": "1bdc8449_968cb492",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86d726d0_570680e5",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T16:54:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Everything goes out of the window if we use a separate permission check, things become a lot simpler from there.\n\nThe callpath I am thinking of is:\n\nInstaller package sets override on installed package -\u003e callingUid is worked through, all good.\nOverride is stored.\nApp gets updated and recheck override is triggered.\nNow in order to validate again that the original caller is allowed to set those overrides we need the original caller, but they didn\u0027t trigger the recheck, so we need to store their uid somewhere and inject it into here.",
      "parentUuid": "b1f8129a_251cae51",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1fbaa5f8_6b521a86",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1431994
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T17:12:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, the first time the override is added, the call path will go through OverridevalidatorImpl ; the second time it will be through CompatConfig.recheckOverrides (and currently that eventually ends up in the same place).\nWhat if instead of storing the uid that made the initial override call, we just store a boolean that remembers whether the initial caller was the installer itself (or had the adequate permission)?",
      "parentUuid": "86d726d0_570680e5",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2624324b_490f1eec",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/compat/OverrideValidatorImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T17:48:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two things:\na) What\u0027s the benefit of storing the boolean over the uid? In that case, we could also just assume that the override got here because the original caller was allowed to and not recheck in the future.\n\nb) There is a case where an app gets updated by a different installer (as happened in the CTS tests). Storing a uid we can recheck, but storing a boolean we cannot. Now this is a bit of an edge case",
      "parentUuid": "1fbaa5f8_6b521a86",
      "revId": "645ba4de9034d1a74197d3705270ac257edf7ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
